# Build output. Everything here is reproducible from source via tools/build.sh,
# including the stage-0 interpreter, the runtime objects, intermediate bootstrap
# stages, and scratch files.
build/

# Scratch space for agents: every temporary file, program, and log goes here,
# never outside the workspace (.cursor/rules/local-tmp.mdc). The directory is
# kept; its contents are not.
tmp/*
!tmp/.gitkeep

# Compiled artifacts, in case any escape build/.
*.o
*.dSYM/

# Per-task planning notes. Transient by nature and superseded by README.md and
# spec/changelog.md once work lands. Agent skills in .cursor/skills/ ARE
# tracked, since they are project governance rather than scratch work.
.cursor/plans/

# Claude Code's per-user settings. .claude/skills is a symlink into .cursor/,
# and .claude/rules holds tracked copies of .cursor/rules, kept in step by
# hand.
.claude/settings.local.json

# macOS and editor noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Do NOT add the patterns below, however tempting a generic template makes it.
#
#   *.out  *.err  *.exit  *.in      golden test expectations in tests/
#   *.ll                            hand-written ABI tests in tests/backend/,
#                                   and eventually bootstrap/stage2.ll, which
#                                   is the only way to build the compiler once
#                                   stage0/ is deleted
#
# These extensions normally mean "build output", but here they define what
# correct behavior is. Ignoring them would make tools/test.sh pass against
# nothing on a fresh clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Toolchain artifacts produced by tools/install.sh --into lib
lib/l0c
lib/l0rt.o
lib/l0host.o
lib/libl0rt.a
lib/L0.md
lib/virt/
